  "notes": [
    "Class pools are distinct trainerName values grouped by trainerClass; gender follows trainerPic and encounterMusic_gender.",
    "Rematches are deduplicated. Canonical leaders, rivals, protagonists, admins and Frontier bosses are excluded; generic class labels and pairs are not first names.",
    "Bug Maniac supplements Bug Catcher; Cue Ball supplements Biker; Super Nerd and Engineer supplement Scientist.",
    "Grunts in these sources have no usable personal names, so selection uses the broad gender or neutral fallback.",
    "Male and female fallbacks collect names from generic trainer classes in both sources. Neutral names are a separately curated unisex pool.",
    "Selection keeps class names first and supplements a short class pool to at least 48 distinct names using the appropriate fallback. No external fetch is used at runtime."
  ],
